# CombatMode Architecture and Style

Ownership detail lives in **Lua file headers**. Load order: **`STRUCTURE.md`** + **`CombatMode/Embeds.xml`**. Prefer Blizzard APIs + `local _, CM = ...`.

## Folder map

- `CombatMode/CombatMode.toc` — metadata, `SavedVariables: CombatModeDB`
- `CombatMode/Embeds.xml` — script load order + root frame `OnEvent` / `OnUpdate`
- `CombatMode/Constants/` — static tables (`Namespace.lua` first)
- `CombatMode/Core/{Runtime,FreeLook,Crosshair,ClickCasting,PartyRadial,Dev}/` — runtime by domain; `Dev/` holds developer tools (profiler) with no production impact when idle
- `CombatMode/UI/{Options,Changelog,Editors}/` — options toolkit/tabs, in-game changelog, secondary editors
- `CombatMode/Bindings.xml` — keybind declarations

## Watch-outs (read the file header for full ownership)

- **CVarManager** — all addon `SetCVar` writes; prior snapshot capture/restore; reticle presets + overrides; Interaction HUD SoftTarget subset.
- **FreeLookController** — mouselook lock/unlock; centering `0 → MouselookStart → deferred 1`; OPie rematch latch; sheath debounce.
- **BindingOverrides** — click-cast / Target Lock secure buttons; Cycle Lock Next/Previous as dedicated Bindings.xml keys (`ApplyCycleFocusBindings` + `SetOverrideBindingClick`; defaults Shift+mouse-wheel).
- **Crosshair companions** — Interaction HUD and Assisted Combat are separate modules under subfolders. Interaction HUD: `Core/Crosshair/InteractionHUD/` — `Target` → `Visual` (fade/range) → `HUD` (chrome + public APIs). Assisted Combat: `Core/Crosshair/AssistedHighlight/` — `Keybinds` → `Motion` (ProcLoop/glow/fade) → `CastProgress` (swipe/break) → `Feedback` (press/pulse + façade; Attach also binds CastProgress) → `Assist` (chrome + public APIs). `FocusNameplateMarker` — when `CM.DB.global.showTargetLockMarker` (default on): Target Lock makes center reticle a static base-colored `crosshairDot` (unreactive) for as long as focus exists (even with no nameplate); hostile-red hit marker reverse-arrives onto the plate (scale/alpha), then color-pulses while settled; parented to plate root with ignore-parent-alpha so bar fades do not stack; plate recycle resumes settled (no re-arrive). Unlock/toggle-off restores reactive reticle. Not `Animations.lua` (reticle cast feedback only).
- **Party Radial companions** — `Core/PartyRadial/` — `PartyData` (roster + `RadialState` / `GetState`) → `SecureBindings` (slice attrs) → `HealthBars` → `RoleIcons` → `Visual` (frames/geometry/slice paint) → `Lifecycle` (show/hide/fade/preview/freelook) → `PartyRadial` (façade; public `CM.PartyRadial` API). Static layout/fade/health-bar sizes + role atlases in `Constants/PartyRadial.lua` (`PartyRadialLayout`, `PartyRadialHealthBar`).
- **Options** — standalone `CombatModeOptionsFrame` (`CM.OpenOptions` / `/cm`), not Blizzard settings; tabs wire to existing `CM.*` + `CM.DB` only.

## Coding conventions

- Per-file global aliases only (no shared `CM.API` alias module). Header order: AddOn namespace (`local _, CM = ...`; Runtime uses `local addonName, CM = ...`) → WoW API → Lua stdlib → module locals. Do not use `local CM = _G.CM`.
- Centralize events via `Constants/Gameplay.lua` + `EventRouter`; no ad-hoc event frames.
- Extend existing `CM` APIs; keep DB scope intentional (`CM.DB.global` vs `CM.DB.char`).
- New settings → matching `UI/Options/Tabs/Tab*.lua` via `ctx:*` helpers + `CM.UI.Options.AddTab`.
- Preserve slash commands and keybinds unless explicitly changing them.
- Lint: `pwsh ./scripts/lint-changed.ps1` (full `pre-commit run --all-files` only for release / explicit request).

## Durable runtime notes

Record non-obvious fixes here (or in `combatmode-lua-safety.mdc`) — one place.

- **Root frame events:** `CombatMode_OnEvent(self, event, ...)` — first arg is the frame, not the event name.
- **DB shape:** AceDB-compatible (`CombatModeDB.global` + `char["Name - Realm"]`); defaults merge in `CM.InitDatabase`.
- **Cast feedback:** Animations outer `OnUpdate` (one motion); terminals via `CM.NotifyCrosshairCastTerminal`; gated by `crosshairCastFeedback`.
- **Assisted Combat matching:** short recent-suggestion cache — `GetNextCastSpell` often advances before `UNIT_SPELLCAST_SUCCEEDED`.
- **FlipBook / atlas VFX:** Ship rows/cols/frames/duration next to the atlas constant in the owning Lua file (see `AssistedHighlight/Motion.lua` for `UF-RogueCP-Slash-Blue`). `C_Texture.GetAtlasInfo` does **not** return FlipBook grid layout. To discover or verify: (1) TextureAtlasViewer / Blizzard UI source (`wow-ui-source`) FlipBook XML for that atlas, (2) other retail addons that already call `SetFlipBookRows` / `SetFlipBookColumns` / `SetFlipBookFrames` + duration on the same atlas name, (3) confirm visually in-game. Do **not** vendor wow-ui-source trees or atlas catalogs into this repo.
- **Options preview:** tab `onSelect`/`onDeselect`; Crosshair → `CM.SetCrosshairOptionsPreview`; Party Radial → `CM.PartyRadial.SetOptionsPreview` (layout-only). Do not reuse mouselook-gated Show/Hide.
- **Function Profiler (`Core/Dev/FunctionProfiler.lua`):** lightweight wrapper around `C_AddOnProfiler.MeasureCall`. Toggle Debug Mode ON in the options panel to start profiling, OFF to dump report + CPU stats to chat. `CM.Profile(key, func, ...)` wraps individual calls; when profiling is off (`CM.profilingEnabled == nil`) the wrapper is a transparent pass-through with zero overhead. `CM.StartProfiling()` / `CM.StopAndReportProfiling()` available as public APIs. Keep wrappers in production code — disabled path is free, and leaving them in avoids needing a code change to re-profile.
- **Options theme:** monochrome via `UI.StripColors`; gold accent (`#E0B847`) for headers / selected tab; toggle tracks use green on / grey off (`UI.Colors.toggleOn` / `trackOff`).

## Change expectations

- Edit the owning module; keep headers accurate when ownership moves. Default header shape for every Lua file: What it does / Architecture / Does not / Related (see docs-sync rule).
- Call out behavior changes that affect mouselook, targeting CVars, or binding overrides.
